      "id": "texture-monophony-to-polyphony",
      "title": "Texture: Monophony to Polyphony",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** theory-advanced | **Difficulty:** 3/10 | **Time:** ~12 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Texture describes how many melodic lines sound simultaneously and their relationship."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monophony",
      "title": "Monophony",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Single melodic line — unison singing, solo whistle, plainchant. No harmony."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "homophony",
      "title": "Homophony",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Melody with chordal accompaniment — most pop, classical melody+accompaniment, hymnody."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "polyphony",
      "title": "Polyphony",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Multiple independent melodies — fugue, round, session twin-fiddle countermelody."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "heterophony",
      "title": "Heterophony",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Same melody simultaneously with slight variations — common in non-Western traditions and informal group singing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "density",
      "title": "Density",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Thin (solo) vs thick (full orchestra tutti). Arrangers control density for emotional arc."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
